# Workout Services

- **Scope**: Start/stop sessions, log sets, detect PRs, compute summaries.
- **Non-Goals**: Long-term analytics (delegate to analytics), scheduling (planning).

## Rules

- Validate user and workout existence via repository protocols.
- Record state transitions at INFO with identifiers and parameters (exercise_id, weight, reps, rpe).
- Invoke `domain_logic` for estimations; do not duplicate formulas.

## Details

ExerciseService
- Create exercise definitions (name, muscles, equipment, mechanics, movement)
- Prevent duplicates with same name + mechanics + equipment + movement
- Search via repo (muscle_groups/equipment filters)

SessionService
- start_workout(user_id, title/notes)
- add_exercise(workout_id, exercise_id, order_index >= 0)
- complete_workout(workout_id, session_rpe, duration_seconds)

TrackingService
- log_set(workout_exercise_id, set_number >= 1, weight_kg/reps/rpe/is_failure)
- evaluate_prs(user_id, exercise_id, weight_kg, reps) → create only on improvement (blended 1RM)

